Bound the lookup of a title bar button colour

The colour table of the title bar buttons holds three blocks of nine
entries. The reader accepts a file with one block or two blocks, and it
clears the icon colour flag for one block alone. A file with two blocks
therefore keeps the flag, and the paint of an inactive window then asks
for the entries eighteen to twenty six. The paint reads the table with
the inserting operator of the map. The icon then takes an invalid colour,
and a paint of the constant style writes nine entries into the live
options.

The style now finds the entry, and it falls back to the colour of a
configuration with no user colours. The dialog reads the same table in
this manner. The reader also completes a short table from the block of
the active window. An older QtCurve painted that block in both window
states. A full table of twenty seven entries paints as before.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 8 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

